{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1369920-suggestions-for-chaos-magic-random-spell-sorcerous-merit","id":1369920,"title":"Suggestions for \"Chaos magic / random spell\" sorcerous merit?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-23T16:00:01-08:00","id":1369920,"title":"Suggestions for \"Chaos magic / random spell\" sorcerous merit?","content":"One of my players wants a sorcerous initiation that combines features of both the Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes and Raksi's tutelage. Our current framework is a &quot;chaos crystal&quot; that he won from gambling with a Fair Folk, which gives him a shaping ritual similar to the Raksi one where you introduce a little chaos into the Spell so that it doesn't go exactly as intended.<br /> <br /> The part I'm hung up on is that he also wants access to a merit like Raksi's Book of Three Circles, allowing him to cast a spell he doesn't know once per story. I don't want to do a direct port of that since I feel like it doesn't properly fit the chaos theme he's going for. Instead, I'd like to have an element of randomness to the unknown spell. The problem though is balancing that randomness with actually being useful when needed.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit torn how how best to accomplish this. The two ideas I currently have is that the crystal randomly picks a spell once per day (or so) which the sorcerer can cast if he wants; if he does, the crystal takes until the end of the story to recharge with a new random spell. Alternatively, when the sorcerer wants to cast an unknown spell, he picks a certain theme and shapes a random spell. For example, if he picked &quot;attack&quot; as his theme, he wouldn't know if he's casting Obsidian Butterflies, Brilliant Raptor, Flying Guillotine, etc., until he finished shaping it.<br /> <br /> Suggestions for improving either of these options or for other alternatives are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-24T09:19:03-08:00","id":1370070,"title":"","content":"You could do a combination of your ideas, actually, relying on Exalted's narrative conventions. Here's what I mean: the crystal picks a spell randomly each day. The sorcerer can at any point roll (Intelligence + Occult) on it, and use the successes they get to either ask the ST what the spell is, or use twice as many successes to just define it. In-story, either way the crystal is still picking randomly, it's just that a skilled sorcerer is also a <i>lucky</i> sorcerer, for whom narrative convenience operates more easily, and thus a good Occult roll can represent the crystal happening to randomly select the spell the sorcerer needs right now.<br /> <br /> A suggested breakdown for the categories:<br /> 1st: The broad &quot;class&quot; of the spell (attack, defense, mobility, communication, transformation, summoning, other)<br /> 2nd: The type of essence the spell uses, expressed by Incarnae type (Elemental Dragons covers anything heavily elemental; Lunar is stuff that deals with animals, plants, or transformations; Maidens cover stuff that curses or blesses without other obvious mechanisms, and protection from sorcery; Solar handles big non- or mixed-elemental attacks, anything &quot;holy&quot;, and summoning non-demon, non-elemental creatures (because the Sun is In Charge); Neverborn covers pure death and Underworld magic; and Yozis covers demonic stuff).<br /> 3rd: The general effect of the spell (&quot;it's a single-target attack&quot;, &quot;it will transport you a short distance quickly&quot;, &quot;it will defend you and your friends&quot;, etc.)<br /> 4th: The specific spell. <br /> <br /> I'd charge successively more successes for each category: 1 for the 1st, 2 for the 2nd, 3 for the 3rd, and 4 for the 4th, or double that to pick them. So just knowing your spell exactly would cost 10 successes, while <i>picking</i> precisely what you need is 20. That seems sufficiently tough that the sorcerer would very rarely get it exactly, but could occasionally pull it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}